WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.324 --> 00:00:14.649
Zann Perda rushed back to the main room.

2
00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:18.551
Elbi was staring out the window, along with the students and the Void.

3
00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:20.772
The young researcher had disappeared.

4
00:00:21.472 --> 00:00:23.693
A second later he zapped back into the lab.

5
00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:26.214
"Everything's okay," he announced.

6
00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:30.516
"I went to the palace square to see what's going on; it's just another protest.

7
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.141
The anti-Reds set off a banner cloud that said 'Letting Reds rule is inside out!

8
00:00:36.942 --> 00:00:38.282
Brains matter more than hair.'"

9
00:00:38.302 --> 00:00:41.503
"Ugh." Elbi rolled her eyes.

10
00:00:41.523 --> 00:00:44.204
"There've been so many protests lately.

11
00:00:44.604 --> 00:00:46.384
I'm getting really tired of them."

12
00:00:47.184 --> 00:00:48.245
The Void glanced over.

13
00:00:48.265 --> 00:00:51.946
"The protests only started yesterday," she reminded Elbi.

14
00:00:51.966 --> 00:00:55.887
"And some people think the anti-Reds' concerns are valid."

15
00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:58.528
Just then one of the students shouted.

16
00:00:58.548 --> 00:00:59.568
"My notes!"

17
00:01:00.872 --> 00:01:04.054
Zann turned and saw Zing standing near some burning papers.

18
00:01:04.074 --> 00:01:07.657
"Oops, sorry about that," said Zann.

19
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:10.199
"He shoots flames when he's startled."

20
00:01:10.939 --> 00:01:12.380
The student glared at Zing.

21
00:01:13.061 --> 00:01:15.303
Rubbing his hands together, he touched his papers.

22
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:23.889
"Restore!" "We should probably go before Zing burns the whole place down," Perda whispered to Zann.

23
00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:26.471
"We can come back tomorrow and talk to Olpa."

24
00:01:27.611 --> 00:01:28.252
Zann nodded.

25
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.844
Nothing in the closet had looked like a clue, except maybe that weird bird sculpture.

26
00:01:33.564 --> 00:01:36.987
But still, he wished he didn't have to wait until tomorrow to find out more.

27
00:01:37.748 --> 00:01:40.470
Zann and Perda thanked Elbi and then hurried outside with Zing.

28
00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:44.953
"Let's go see how Darb and Gliss are doing at the zoo," Perda suggested.

29
00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.816
Zann sighed and glanced back at the lab.

30
00:01:47.836 --> 00:01:49.797
"Okay," he said.

31
00:01:50.498 --> 00:01:51.599
He rubbed his fingers together.

32
00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:55.382
"Zap!" Splash!

33
00:01:55.402 --> 00:01:57.844
"Drat," Zann grumbled.

34
00:01:58.572 --> 00:02:01.234
He climbed out of the zoo's fishpond and rubbed his hands together.

35
00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.895
"Dry," said Zann, placing his hands on his pants.

36
00:02:05.636 --> 00:02:07.277
He felt a small lump in his pocket.

37
00:02:07.297 --> 00:02:08.557
"Double drat!"

38
00:02:08.918 --> 00:02:09.538
Zann mumbled.

39
00:02:10.238 --> 00:02:12.219
Perda appeared just in time to hear him.

40
00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:13.740
"What's wrong?"

41
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:14.561
she asked.

42
00:02:14.581 --> 00:02:18.103
"I meant to ask someone at the lab about this."

43
00:02:18.983 --> 00:02:20.884
Zann pulled out the stone Wyssa had given him.

44
00:02:20.904 --> 00:02:24.966
"I thought they might know if it came from a different magical world.

45
00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:28.048
I think it's a clue to where my parents are."

46
00:02:28.736 --> 00:02:30.037
"You still have that?"

47
00:02:30.377 --> 00:02:31.398
Perda looked surprised.

48
00:02:31.418 --> 00:02:34.020
"I thought Wyssa told you to give it to Boz."

49
00:02:35.401 --> 00:02:36.061
Zann shrugged.

50
00:02:36.562 --> 00:02:37.923
"I haven't had a chance yet.

51
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:41.245
He's been really busy, in case you haven't noticed."

52
00:02:41.985 --> 00:02:42.686
Perda frowned.

53
00:02:42.706 --> 00:02:47.869
"We've been running around looking for clues, but that stone might be the only clue you need!

54
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.531
You really should ask Boz about it."

55
00:02:51.332 --> 00:02:51.752
"I will."

56
00:02:52.192 --> 00:02:53.914
Zann put the stone back in his pocket.

57
00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.956
"Look, Darb and Gliss are over there."

58
00:02:57.612 --> 00:03:01.013
Darb had volunteered to help restore the wild dragon pen at the zoo.

59
00:03:02.253 --> 00:03:03.494
He knew a lot about dragons.

60
00:03:03.914 --> 00:03:06.734
Gliss was helping him by providing the magic to make repairs.

61
00:03:07.495 --> 00:03:09.415
They looked up when Zann and Perda approached.

62
00:03:09.435 --> 00:03:13.176
"Good, you're here," Gliss said with a weary sigh.

63
00:03:13.196 --> 00:03:16.897
"We've been working hard since lunchtime, and I'm exhausted.

64
00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.578
I could use your help creating friction."

65
00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.279
"Did you learn anything useful at the lab?"

66
00:03:22.519 --> 00:03:23.479
Darb asked Zann.

67
00:03:23.499 --> 00:03:24.999
"Not really."

68
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.900
Zann filled him in on what had happened.

69
00:03:28.064 --> 00:03:31.265
"I wonder what the burnt bird sculpture is," Darb said.

70
00:03:32.006 --> 00:03:34.027
He was interested in anything related to animals.

71
00:03:34.787 --> 00:03:38.128
He even seemed to get along with Teplo's ill-tempered sniffer goose.

72
00:03:38.929 --> 00:03:44.411
Zann and Darb, as well as Boz, had been staying at Teplo's house since Morb had disappeared, and

73
00:03:44.431 --> 00:03:47.772
the goose still honked suspiciously every time she saw Zann.

74
00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:50.474
"I don't know," Zann told Darb.

75
00:03:50.494 --> 00:03:53.535
"I'm not even sure the sculpture belonged to my parents.

76
00:03:54.655 --> 00:03:55.796
I never saw it before.

77
00:03:56.528 --> 00:03:58.990
Maybe someone put it on their shelf by mistake."

78
00:03:59.951 --> 00:04:02.393
Perda held out her hands to join friction with Gliss.

79
00:04:02.413 --> 00:04:06.016
"You can ask about it when we go back to the lab tomorrow."

80
00:04:06.797 --> 00:04:07.637
Zann sighed.

81
00:04:07.657 --> 00:04:12.061
"I hope Boz doesn't zap us back to Swamp Bottom before tomorrow."

82
00:04:12.861 --> 00:04:14.863
He clenched his fists with frustration.

83
00:04:14.883 --> 00:04:16.845
"I can't go back!

84
00:04:17.225 --> 00:04:20.608
There aren't any wormholes within a day's walk of Swamp Bottom."

85
00:04:21.388 --> 00:04:23.250
"Wormholes?" Gliss said.

86
00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.692
"Why do you need to be near a wormhole?"

87
00:04:26.736 --> 00:04:27.356
Zann shrugged.

88
00:04:27.376 --> 00:04:29.617
"My parents disappeared in one."

89
00:04:30.357 --> 00:04:31.878
Gliss gave Zann a funny look.

90
00:04:31.898 --> 00:04:36.379
"Yeah, but it's not as if you can just jump into a wormhole to look for them."

91
00:04:36.399 --> 00:04:37.819
"Why not?"

92
00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:39.080
Zann shrugged again.

93
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.440
"Maybe I should do exactly that!"

94
00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.181
"Really?" Perda sounded excited.

95
00:04:44.201 --> 00:04:49.342
"Hey, that reminds me—you promised to tell us what it was like when Wyssa took you through the

96
00:04:49.362 --> 00:04:51.843
wormhole!" Gliss ignored her.

97
00:04:51.863 --> 00:04:53.944
"You can't be serious, Zann!"

98
00:04:54.344 --> 00:04:54.804
she cried.

99
00:04:55.624 --> 00:04:58.486
"Wormholes are way too dangerous to mess around with."

100
00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:00.908
"She's right," Darb said.

101
00:05:00.928 --> 00:05:05.952
"Jumping into a wormhole isn't exactly a smart plan for finding your parents."

102
00:05:06.953 --> 00:05:09.836
"Well, it's the only plan I've got," said Zann.

103
00:05:10.896 --> 00:05:12.538
"Not really," Perda said.

104
00:05:12.558 --> 00:05:15.660
"You haven't shown Boz that stone, remember?

105
00:05:16.101 --> 00:05:19.543
Maybe that would—" "You haven't shown Boz what stone?"

106
00:05:20.124 --> 00:05:21.425
a familiar voice interrupted.

107
00:05:22.206 --> 00:05:23.146
Zann spun around.

108
00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:24.988
"Boz!" he exclaimed.

109
00:05:25.684 --> 00:05:27.545
His grandfather had just zapped into view.

110
00:05:27.865 --> 00:05:28.685
Teplo was with him.

111
00:05:28.705 --> 00:05:30.585
"Hello, kids."

112
00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:32.546
Teplo greeted them with a smile.

113
00:05:33.206 --> 00:05:37.487
"We came to let you know that we're all invited to dinner at Saffa's house tonight.

114
00:05:38.148 --> 00:05:39.488
We're meeting there in an hour."

115
00:05:40.188 --> 00:05:42.029
Boz wasn't paying attention to Teplo.

116
00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:43.549
He was still looking at Zann.

117
00:05:43.569 --> 00:05:45.090
"What stone?"

118
00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.150
he said again.

119
00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.391
"Zann?" Zann pulled out the stone.

120
00:05:50.111 --> 00:05:53.964
He explained how Wyssa had told him to pass it on to Boz.

121
00:05:53.984 --> 00:05:56.206
"Could it be a clue to where my parents are?"

122
00:05:56.566 --> 00:05:57.167
Zann asked.

123
00:05:58.127 --> 00:05:59.449
Teplo leaned in for a look.

124
00:05:59.969 --> 00:06:02.171
One bushy eyebrow shot up in surprise.

125
00:06:02.191 --> 00:06:05.213
"Why, that's a—" Zip!

126
00:06:05.573 --> 00:06:10.117
A flash of energy shot from Boz's fingertips, sealing Teplo's lips shut.

127
00:06:10.858 --> 00:06:13.039
Teplo's eyes widened in surprise.

128
00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.941
Boz turned to Zann.

129
00:06:14.961 --> 00:06:20.065
"Wyssa can't be trusted," he said grimly, plucking the stone from Zann's hand.

130
00:06:20.085 --> 00:06:22.587
"This stone means nothing."
